ave for a few bosses that requires some  Loosli time quick time events to  vanquish there is one new addition to  battles here in some levels characters  can duck behind cover and shoot at  enemies but the game's concessions to a  younger audience make this addition  challenge free hitting the left trigger  automatically targets an enemy so  there's never any need to actually aim  the Lego formula may be well traveled by  now but it's still a pleasant one to  experience even though a lot of your  enjoyment will depend on your affinity  with the Star Wars universe simple  though they might be I still found alive  in many of Lego Star Wars levels it was  exciting flying poe dameron's x-wing for  example dogfighting against waves of TIE  fighters emits chatter from my fellow  pilots  you want to keep for yourself  and while the goofiness in mr. Lego  games approach their source material has  now become somewhat rote it's still  elicited a few laughs from me  there are even several extra levels that  expanding the events from the film for  Star Wars fans these are exciting  additions and it's given more  authenticity by the inclusion of nearly  the entire cast of The Force awakens who  recorded new lines of dialogue for the  game it's wonderful if your style was  completionist but it's also annoying as  these new non-film levels are hard to  access they're locked away until you  earned the requisite number of gold  bricks within the game so you're going  to need to play a lot of lego star wars  to experience them all but playing a lot  of Lego Star Wars The Force awakens  won't be a chore especially if you do  have a younger partner to take with you  in your galactic journey lego star wars  the force awakens doesn't really take  you to a new galaxy far far away but  it's still a pleasant journey han Solo
 

